Short:        WebKit JavaScript engine for AmigaOS 3.2
Author:       Dalsin Limited
Uploader:     UPLOADER-PLACEHOLDER
Type:         comm/www
Version:      0.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2
Distribution: Aminet

OpenBrowser is a web browser for AmigaOS 3.2, built on WebKit. This first
release is its JavaScript engine only: WebKit's JavaScriptCore (JSC), the
"jsc" shell, ported to AmigaOS 3.2 on the 68020 and up with an FPU.

    jsc -e "print(1+1)"
    jsc script.js

What works: the C-loop interpreter (no JIT), functions, objects, arrays,
strings, JSON, RegExp, Date, exceptions and full double-precision maths.

Requirements:
  - AmigaOS 3.2 or newer
  - 68020 or better with an FPU (68881/68882/68040/68060)
  - about 80 MB of free Fast RAM (the program is 71 MB)
  - Stack 4194304 (4 MB) in the shell before running it

Not yet: web pages. The browser window (GadTools), image support through
datatypes and page drawing come next.

